{
  "_doc": [
    "Semantic lexicon for enterprise-material comprehension.",
    "",
    "This file was ABSENT. _semantic_lexicon() loads it with a {} default, so every one of",
    "the 19 _lexicon_* call sites across _parsing.py, _utils.py, business_state_graph.py and",
    "supplementary_behavior_slices.py silently received an empty list or dict. An entire",
    "policy-driven comprehension layer was inert, and two of its failure modes are worse than",
    "a gap: with no forbidden_transition_markers a FORBIDDEN transition is classified as an",
    "ALLOWED one, so the product asserts the transition should succeed and reports a false",
    "defect when the target correctly refuses it; with no positive_integer_markers the typed",
    "constraint extractor returns {} unconditionally.",
    "",
    "WHAT BELONGS HERE: document-structure and language vocabulary -- how enterprise material",
    "SAYS things. Section headings, grant/deny phrasing, ownership scoping, comparison words,",
    "and cross-language equivalents for common business nouns.",
    "",
    "WHAT DOES NOT BELONG HERE: any customer's business rules, entity semantics, or",
    "industry-specific taxonomy. This file must never encode what a defect IS, only how a",
    "document expresses a fact. Deployments extend it for their own vocabulary; that",
    "extensibility is what keeps the vocabulary out of the code.",
    "",
    "entity_token_lexicon is a LANGUAGE aid, not an industry model: without cross-language",
    "noun equivalence a Chinese-language PRD cannot have its state-machine subject resolved at",
    "all, which would restrict the product to English material -- a far worse coupling than a",
    "translation table. Add terms for the language a deployment actually receives."
  ],
