  "_verb_action_lexicon_shape": [
    "KEY is the word as a document writes it; VALUE is the canonical action it maps to.",
    "This is the same direction as entity_token_lexicon, and it matters: the consumer does",
    "actions.extend(target_tokens) on a match, so a {canonical: [synonyms...]} shape would",
    "emit every synonym as a granted action. A permission row would then claim actions the",
    "document never granted, and obligations would be compiled for them -- exactly the",
    "over-broad inference the evidence rules forbid. A canonical word maps to itself."
  ],
